# Phase 999.17 — trivy suppression baseline. Body intentionally empty.
# See .planning/phases/999.17-devsecops-shift-left-security-tooling/.
#
# .trivyignore — CVE IDs and check IDs Trivy should not flag.
#
# FORMAT (one per line):
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN                  # vulnerability scan
#   AVD-DS-NNNN                      # misconfiguration scan
#   <secret-rule-id>                 # secret scan
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD    # with expiration date
#
# RULES:
# 1. Every entry MUST have a comment line above it with:
#    (a) the reason this is accepted (no impact in our settings, fix not yet
#        available, etc.)
#    (b) a ticket / issue link, and
#    (c) a re-evaluate-by date.
# 2. Use exp:YYYY-MM-DD when you accept a finding for a bounded window.
# 3. Empty file = clean state.
#
# Example (commented out — uncomment + populate when needed):
# # No impact: this is a Dockerfile linting rule that flags HEALTHCHECK
# # absence, but our entrypoint container is upstream-managed.
# # See: https://internal-tracker/issue/123 — re-evaluate 2026-09-01
# AVD-DS-0026 exp:2026-09-01
